<title>ISRAEL: Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</title>
<headline>Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following shipments of grain have arrived or are due to arrive in Israeli ports, according to the inspection agency Hevra Klalit Lehashgaha (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel	     ETA	   Cargo	    Quantity   Origin</p>
<p>Unlo		 unloading   sunflower meal  2,500     Europe</p>
<p>Floriana	   unloading   barley	   11,261     Europe</p>
<p>Peleduy	    25/11	 sunflowerseed   1,740     Europe</p>
<p>Bodaibo	    26/11	 rapeseeds	 2,200     Ukraine</p>
<p>Mecanik Vak	28/11	 barley	    3,746     Europe</p>
<p>Grigorousa	 28/11	 sorghum	  14,426     U.S.</p>
<p>				     soya	     15,517</p>
<p>				     corn		7,510</p>
<p>Volgobal 186     29/11	 bran		2,550     Europe</p>
<p>Volgobal 191     30/11	 sunflower meal  2,000     Europe</p>
<p>Volzky 32	   1/12	 fodder wheat    3,500     Europe</p>
<p>Antalya	     3/12	 maize grits     2,500     Europe</p>
<p>Yoanis		5/12	 wheat	    34,397     U.S.</p>
<p>				     soya	     24,230</p>
<p>Federal Dora     16/12	 barley+feed    25,000     U.S.</p>
<p>					 wheat</p>
<p>Liberty Sea	20/12	 na		 60,000     U.S.</p>
